d 'BJ': module to to implement the Box-Jenkins strategy (identification, estimation, diagnostic checking and forecast) in two figures
d
d  bj gathers the steps of the Box-Jenkins time series strategy in
d a single command. The output consists of two figures. The first
d (identification) displays the time plot of the series, its
d autocorrelation and partial autocorrelation functions,
d descriptive statistics, Dickey-Fuller unit root tests and ARMA
d order selection by AIC, BIC and HQIC. The second (estimation)
d displays observed and fitted values, a forecast, the residuals,
d their histogram, a normal Q-Q plot and residual diagnostics
d (Ljung-Box, McLeod-Li, Jarque-Bera). The model can be the one
d selected by BIC or any arima specification given by the user,
d including covariates. It is intended for teaching and applied
d analysis. 
d
d KW: Box-Jenkins
d KW: ARIMA
d
d Requires: Stata version 18
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261125
d
d Author: Rodrigo Taborda,  Universidad de los Andes
d Support: email r.taborda@@uniandes.edu.co
d
f bj.ado
f bj.sthlp
f bj_test_simple.do
